WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.110
Speaker 1: Let's now take some phone calls.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.930
We're going to hear from people in the audience.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.310
We do this via discord.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.670
They're not really phone calls, but sometimes
it's kind of like hard to explain what they

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.429
are if I don't say phone calls.

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:11.550
So I just call in phone calls.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:18.500
But you go to David Pakman dot com slash discord
and that's where it's all happening.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.520
All right.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:26.760
Let's go with Adrian from Wyoming and hear
from Adrian first today.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.340
Adrian, what's going on?

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.380
Speaker 3: Hi, David.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:36.970
I have a question for you about what Joe Biden
cares about, because I know there's kind of

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.340
a maxim about if presidents really care about
certain issues, they'll do more.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.770
And I'm wondering how you think he's done
regarding trans rights, especially in the

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:52.700
wake of the potential expulsion of a montana
state senator today.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.350
I don't know exactly what's going on with
that.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.309
Speaker 1: I did not see that story.

00:00:57.309 --> 00:00:58.420
But let me address that.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.590
You know, here's here's the thing.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:07.620
With all of these issues, so often this debate
starts about has the president done enough

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.750
or not on a particular issue?

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:15.229
And then subsequent to that, the question
becomes how much can a president do about

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:17.070
that particular issue?

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:23.290
And when it comes to trans issues, the unfortunate
reality is that a lot of this stuff is determined

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.409
at the state level.

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:31.070
Now, you could say, well, there should be
some overarching federal law protecting trans

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:36.940
people, but we already know from experience
with other issues related to gender and sexual

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.930
orientation that that often is not something
that happens or happens quickly.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:46.979
So I have to admit, I don't know the full
scope of what Biden could do federally to

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:51.320
best evaluate how what kind of a job he's
done, if that makes sense.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.320
Right.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.880
Speaker 3: And I personally but I'm right
with you there.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.969
I realize that in a deadlocked Congress, there's
very little that's potentially going to get

00:01:59.969 --> 00:02:04.900
done, especially with the red meat that this
issue unfortunately provides to the Republican

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:05.900
base.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:06.900
Absolutely.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:14.150
I just think I just wonder and I just wanted
to hear your perspective symbolically, like

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:21.040
like for when he invited the Tennessee three
over earlier, I believe, this week and just

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.650
hosting more events or just talking a little
bit more about those kind of issues just from

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.180
that kind of perspective, because I realize
legislatively that he's kind of deadlocked

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.069
and not much may get done.

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:32.450
But I appreciate your thoughts on.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:37.920
Speaker 1: Well, listen, I mean, okay, so
Biden could sign executive orders and and

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.989
direct federal departments to enact certain
policy protections.

00:02:43.989 --> 00:02:44.989
Okay.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:46.950
So I don't know that he's done a ton of that.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:49.870
He can use the bully pulpit to talk about
the issue.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:53.290
I think he has I mean, he brings up trans
issues at many speeches.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.370
So I think they're he's doing okay.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:03:01.319
He can appoint officials in his administration
who are defenders of trans rights.

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:03.030
And I think mostly he's done that.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.590
He certainly hasn't appointed anyone I'm aware
of who's hostile or indifferent to trans rights.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.709
So that's okay.

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:14.290
And then he can sort of like push state and
local governments to do one thing or the other.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:18.349
But the unfortunate reality is the state,
the state governments that would listen to

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:23.430
Biden are already doing pretty well when it
comes to protecting trans people anyway.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:28.292
And the state governments that are aggressively
persecuting trans people aren't going to care

00:03:28.292 --> 00:03:29.670
what Joe Biden says anyway.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:33.030
So, you know, I think he's doing okay, but
he could always do more.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:36.220
Speaker 3: Yeah, I fully agree.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:40.890
I really appreciate it because I know that
my ex-husband, my ex date where I went to

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:44.560
college in Minnesota, their age took a big
step back.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.799
Everyone's either taking big steps up or big
steps back.

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:49.340
And it's just very unfortunate to see right
now.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.650
So I appreciate you taking the call.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:52.780
Thanks for your perspective.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.010
Hope you have a great day.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.010
Speaker 1: All right.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.010
Thank you.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.640
There is Adrian from Wyoming.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:03.049
